IMPORT prelude

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 5 December 2025 -- PART 2, CONTRACTS OF SERVICE.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/EmA1968.txt
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the text with the writing-l4-rules skill and
-- nothing else: no pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no
-- human gate. Observations, not checked findings.
--
-- SCOPE. Part 2 only -- ss 8 to 14. The Act has 16 Parts and 275,000 characters;
-- Part 2 is the one an ordinary employee meets, because it decides how a job
-- ends and how much notice is owed. Parts 3 (salary), 4 (rest days and hours),
-- 9 (maternity) and 10 (leave) are each at least as useful and none is encoded.
--
-- NOT ENCODED within Part 2: ss 15 to 19 (termination where the employee is
-- threatened by danger, liability on breach, trade union rights, change of
-- employer, transfer of employment, and the offence provision).
--
-- NO DATE TYPE. See the note on service length below: the Act's own thresholds
-- are not in one unit, so the encoding asks the questions the Act asks rather
-- than computing them from dates.

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- Part 2, Contracts of Service`

§§ `10(3) -- how long notice must be`

-- s 10(3): "The notice to terminate the service of a person who is employed
-- under a contract of service must be at least --
--   (a) one day's notice if the person has been so employed for LESS THAN
--       26 WEEKS;
--   (b) one week's notice if the person has been so employed for 26 WEEKS OR
--       MORE but less than 2 YEARS;
--   (c) 2 weeks' notice if the person has been so employed for 2 YEARS OR MORE
--       but less than 5 YEARS; and
--   (d) 4 weeks' notice if the person has been so employed for 5 YEARS OR MORE."
--
-- The three thresholds are 26 weeks, 2 years and 5 years. Those are not in one
-- unit and the Act supplies no conversion, so the encoding does not invent one:
-- each threshold is asked as the Act asks it. Deriving all three from a single
-- day count would require deciding how many days are in two years, which is a
-- question the Act does not answer and which differs across leap years.
DECLARE ServiceLength HAS
    `employed for 26 weeks or more`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed for 2 years or more`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed for 5 years or more`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- The statutory minimum, in days. One week is 7 days and the Act's own units
-- are weeks, so the table converts only within the week/day pair it states.
GIVEN `the service` IS A ServiceLength
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the minimum notice in days under section 10(3)` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the service`'s `employed for 5 years or more`  THEN 28   -- (d) 4 weeks
        IF `the service`'s `employed for 2 years or more`  THEN 14   -- (c) 2 weeks
        IF `the service`'s `employed for 26 weeks or more` THEN 7    -- (b) 1 week
        OTHERWISE 1                                                  -- (a) 1 day

§§ `8 and 10(2) -- the contract, and what happens when it is less favourable`

-- s 10(2): "The length of the notice must be the same for both employer and
-- employee and is to be determined by any provision made for the notice in the
-- terms of the contract of service, or, IN THE ABSENCE OF SUCH PROVISION, must
-- be in accordance with subsection (3)."
--
-- s 8: "Every term of a contract of service which provides a condition of
-- service which is less favourable to an employee than any of the conditions of
-- service prescribed by this Act is ILLEGAL AND VOID to the extent that it is
-- so less favourable."
--
-- Read together these produce a three-step chain, which is the most interesting
-- thing in Part 2:
--   1. the contract's notice period governs (s 10(2));
--   2. unless it is less favourable to the employee than s 10(3), in which case
--      s 8 makes it void to that extent;
--   3. and once it is void there is no provision in the contract, so s 10(2)'s
--      own words -- "in the absence of such provision" -- send the question back
--      to s 10(3).
-- The employee therefore gets the statutory minimum, by a route that passes
-- through three subsections and is nowhere stated in one place.
DECLARE ContractTerms HAS
    `the contract makes provision for notice`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice period the contract provides, in days` IS A NUMBER
    -- s 10(2) first limb: the length "must be the same for both employer and
    -- employee". A contract giving the employer a shorter notice than the
    -- employee is contrary to this, whatever the figures.
    `the contract provides the same length for both parties` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Less favourable TO THE EMPLOYEE means shorter than the statutory minimum.
GIVEN `the terms` IS A ContractTerms, `the service` IS A ServiceLength
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contractual notice is less favourable than the Act` IF
        `the terms`'s `the contract makes provision for notice`
    AND `the terms`'s `the notice period the contract provides, in days`
            LESS THAN `the minimum notice in days under section 10(3)` `the service`

-- s 8 voids it to the extent it is less favourable.
GIVEN `the terms` IS A ContractTerms, `the service` IS A ServiceLength
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contractual notice term is void under section 8` IF
    `the contractual notice is less favourable than the Act` `the terms` `the service`

-- The length that actually governs, after the chain above.
GIVEN `the terms` IS A ContractTerms, `the service` IS A ServiceLength
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the notice period that governs, in days` IS
    IF   `the contract provision stands`  `the terms` `the service`
    THEN `the terms`'s `the notice period the contract provides, in days`
    ELSE `the minimum notice in days under section 10(3)` `the service`

GIVEN `the terms` IS A ContractTerms, `the service` IS A ServiceLength
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract provision stands` IF
        `the terms`'s `the contract makes provision for notice`
    AND NOT `the contractual notice term is void under section 8` `the terms` `the service`

-- s 10(2), first limb, on its own: a term that is not symmetrical does not
-- answer the subsection even if it is generous.
GIVEN `the terms` IS A ContractTerms
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract breaches the equal-length requirement in section 10(2)` IF
        `the terms`'s `the contract makes provision for notice`
    AND NOT `the terms`'s `the contract provides the same length for both parties`

§§ `10(4) and 10(5) -- waiver and the form of the notice`

-- s 10(4): "This section does not prevent either party from waiving that
-- party's right to notice on any occasion."
-- s 10(5): "The notice must be written and may be given at any time, and the
-- day on which the notice is given is INCLUDED in the period of the notice."
--
-- The inclusion rule is why a one-day notice given on Monday expires on Monday:
-- the day of giving counts. Encoded as the arithmetic the subsection states.
DECLARE Notice HAS
    `the notice is in writing`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the length given, in days`     IS A NUMBER
    `the receiving party waived the right to notice` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the notice` IS A Notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice satisfies section 10(5)` IF
    `the notice`'s `the notice is in writing`

-- The number of further days after the day of giving, s 10(5) counting the day
-- of giving itself.
GIVEN `the notice` IS A Notice
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days remaining after the day the notice is given` IS
    `the notice`'s `the length given, in days` MINUS 1

GIVEN `the notice` IS A Notice, `the terms` IS A ContractTerms, `the service` IS A ServiceLength
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is long enough` IF
        `the notice`'s `the receiving party waived the right to notice`
    OR  `the notice`'s `the length given, in days`
            AT LEAST `the notice period that governs, in days` `the terms` `the service`

§§ `11 -- Termination without notice`

-- s 11(1): either party may terminate without notice "by paying to the other
-- party a sum equal to the amount of salary at the gross rate of pay which
-- would have accrued to the employee during the period of the notice".
GIVEN `the gross daily rate of pay` IS A NUMBER
    , `the terms` IS A ContractTerms
    , `the service` IS A ServiceLength
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the payment in lieu of notice` IS
    `the gross daily rate of pay` TIMES (`the notice period that governs, in days` `the terms` `the service`)

-- s 11(2): "Either party ... may terminate the contract of service without
-- notice in the event of any WILFUL BREACH by the other party of a condition of
-- the contract of service." No payment, and no inquiry required -- contrast
-- s 14(1), which does require one.
GIVEN `there was a wilful breach by the other party of a condition of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the party may terminate without notice and without payment under section 11(2)` IF
    `there was a wilful breach by the other party of a condition of the contract`

§§ `13 -- When the contract is deemed broken`

-- s 13(1): "An employer is deemed to have broken the employer's contract of
-- service with the employee if the employer fails to pay salary in accordance
-- with Part 3." One fact, no qualification, no excuse.
GIVEN `the employer failed to pay salary in accordance with Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is deemed to have broken the contract` IF
    `the employer failed to pay salary in accordance with Part 3`

-- s 13(2): "An employee is deemed to have broken the employee's contract of
-- service with the employer if the employee is absent from work for MORE THAN
-- 2 DAYS CONTINUOUSLY without prior leave from the employer AND --
--   (a) the employee has no reasonable excuse for the absence; or
--   (b) the employee does not inform and does not attempt to inform the
--       employer of the excuse for the absence."
--
-- Note the asymmetry with s 13(1): the employer's deemed breach has one
-- element, the employee's has three, and limb (b) is itself a double negative.
DECLARE Absence HAS
    `days absent continuously`                      IS A NUMBER
    `with prior leave from the employer`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee has a reasonable excuse for the absence` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `the employee informed or attempted to inform the employer of the excuse` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)

GIVEN `the absence` IS AN Absence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a limb of section 13(2) is made out` IF
        NOT `the absence`'s `the employee has a reasonable excuse for the absence`
    OR  NOT `the absence`'s `the employee informed or attempted to inform the employer of the excuse`

GIVEN `the absence` IS AN Absence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is deemed to have broken the contract` IF
        `the absence`'s `days absent continuously` GREATER THAN 2
    AND NOT `the absence`'s `with prior leave from the employer`
    AND `a limb of section 13(2) is made out` `the absence`

§§ `14 -- Dismissal`

-- s 14(1): "An employer may AFTER DUE INQUIRY dismiss without notice an
-- employee ... on the grounds of misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of
-- the express or implied conditions of the employee's service, except that
-- instead of dismissing an employee an employer may -- (a) instantly down-grade
-- the employee; or (b) instantly suspend the employee from work without payment
-- of salary for a period NOT EXCEEDING ONE WEEK."
DECLARE DismissalFacts HAS
    `there was misconduct inconsistent with the conditions of service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer held a due inquiry`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee was instead down-graded`      IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `the employee was instead suspended without salary` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `the days of suspension`                    IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DismissalFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer may dismiss without notice under section 14(1)` IF
        `the facts`'s `there was misconduct inconsistent with the conditions of service`
    AND `the facts`'s `the employer held a due inquiry`

-- The lesser measures are alternatives to dismissal and share its precondition:
-- "instead of dismissing an employee an employer may", so due inquiry is needed
-- for these too.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A DismissalFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension is within the section 14(1)(b) limit` IF
    `the facts`'s `the days of suspension` AT MOST 7

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DismissalFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension is lawful under section 14(1)(b)` IF
        `the employer may dismiss without notice under section 14(1)` `the facts`
    AND `the facts`'s `the employee was instead suspended without salary`
    AND `the suspension is within the section 14(1)(b) limit` `the facts`

-- s 14(2A): who may bring a wrongful-dismissal claim. "relevant employee"
-- means --
--   (a) an employee in a managerial or executive position who is dismissed with
--       notice, or without notice but with salary in lieu, AFTER HAVING SERVED
--       THAT EMPLOYER FOR AT LEAST 6 MONTHS in any position;
--   (b) an employee in a managerial or executive position dismissed without
--       notice and without salary in lieu;
--   (c) "an employee not employed in a managerial or an executive position."
--
-- Limb (c) is the whole of its own text: no service qualification, no condition
-- about notice. So every employee outside a managerial or executive position is
-- a relevant employee from the first day, and only managers and executives face
-- any threshold at all.
DECLARE Dismissed HAS
    `in a managerial or an executive position`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `dismissed with notice`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `dismissed without notice but paid salary in lieu` IS A BOOLEAN
    `served that employer for at least 6 months in any position` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the employee` IS A Dismissed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is a relevant employee under section 14(2A)(a)` IF
        `the employee`'s `in a managerial or an executive position`
    AND `dismissed with notice or with salary in lieu` `the employee`
    AND `the employee`'s `served that employer for at least 6 months in any position`

GIVEN `the employee` IS A Dismissed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `dismissed with notice or with salary in lieu` IF
        `the employee`'s `dismissed with notice`
    OR  `the employee`'s `dismissed without notice but paid salary in lieu`

-- (b): the manager dismissed without notice AND without salary in lieu is a
-- relevant employee with NO service qualification at all.
GIVEN `the employee` IS A Dismissed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is a relevant employee under section 14(2A)(b)` IF
        `the employee`'s `in a managerial or an executive position`
    AND NOT `dismissed with notice or with salary in lieu` `the employee`

-- (c): not in a managerial or executive position. One condition, and it is the
-- negation of the condition both other limbs open with.
GIVEN `the employee` IS A Dismissed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is a relevant employee under section 14(2A)(c)` IF
    NOT `the employee`'s `in a managerial or an executive position`

GIVEN `the employee` IS A Dismissed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee may lodge a wrongful dismissal claim` IF
        `the employee is a relevant employee under section 14(2A)(a)` `the employee`
    ..  `the employee is a relevant employee under section 14(2A)(b)` `the employee`
    OR  `the employee is a relevant employee under section 14(2A)(c)` `the employee`
